This page replaced the desk's page for #4471. The old one said: one bug, one fix queued.
Reading every report shows two bugs. This page splits them, one ticket each. The desk
closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser fixed, the hint won't fix.

## What was really merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

379 reports are the parser bug the ticket was opened for — month/day flipped because the
shared parser reads month-first and day-first tenants write day-first. 33 reports are a
different bug: the `booking-v3` form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, people type what the hint says,
and the form reads it day-first. Only channel `form`, only `booking-v3` tenants
(alder.physio de-DE, copper.studio es-ES, pale.harbour pt-PT).

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why the desk saw one problem

- Intake tags disagree with the real cause in 38 of 412 reports: 23 tagged `hint` are
  parser, 15 tagged `parser` are hint. Tag, not tenant+form, drove the merge queue.
- Decision 0001 merges reports on subject lines alone. All of these subjects say the same
  thing ("wrong day", "dates mixed up"), so two bugs merged into one ticket. The decision
  accepted this ("engineering merges them later") — this page is that merge, done.

<Callout kind="warn">
The hint bug was never fixed: the `booking-v3` form was retired instead. Any tenant still
on that form sees flipped dates. A report about it will read as "known" against this page.
</Callout>

## Tickets filed

- [Parser reads dates month-first for day-first locales — 379 reports](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/1)
- [booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY but reads the date day-first — 33 reports](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/2)

